Findings from the POMs (verified, files bihe.pom / rong.pom / cmd64.pom in project root):

- bihe0832: name "LibFFmpegMobile", description "Android APP Factory", scm
  github.com/bihe0832/AndroidAppFactory. This is a component of a general-purpose app
  framework, not a standalone command runner. Declares Apache-2.0 over an FFmpeg payload,
  which is inconsistent: FFmpeg is LGPL at minimum, GPL once libx264 is linked. License
  metadata cannot be trusted. Kotlin stdlib 1.7.10.
- cn.rongcloud.sdk: description "RongCloud Android SDK", url rongcloud.cn. Internal
  component of a commercial chat/RTC vendor SDK. Same Apache-2.0-over-FFmpeg
  inconsistency. No public command API documented. Almost certainly coupled to RongCloud
  SDK internals.
- ffmpeg-cmd64: LGPL-2.1 is the only *plausible* license of the three, BUT the description
  is "Video player based on FFmpeg n4.0.2" and LGPL specifically means libx264 is NOT
  linked (libx264 is GPL; linking it forces the whole build to GPL). Our entire
  FFmpegCommandBuilder passes "-c:v libx264" in every command. An LGPL build cannot honour
  that. Also pins appcompat 1.3.1 / material 1.3.0 (2021).

=> None of the three is a credible drop-in for FFmpegWrapper. ABI inspection is still
   unfinished, but license/function mismatch already disqualifies them on current evidence.
   Do NOT integrate any of them without resolving the above.

